<!doctype html>
<html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Research OS — Recon-Sync</title>
<hta:application id="reconSync" applicationname="Research OS Recon-Sync" border="thin" caption="yes" maximizebutton="yes" minimizebutton="yes" singleinstance="yes"/>
<style>body{font:15px Segoe UI,Arial;background:#101923;color:#eaf1f8;margin:28px}h1{font-size:24px}p{color:#b9c9d9;max-width:820px;line-height:1.5}button{background:#173f5f;color:white;border:1px solid #47799d;border-radius:5px;padding:10px 16px;margin:5px;cursor:pointer}#result{white-space:pre-wrap;background:#0a1118;border:1px solid #344657;padding:14px;margin-top:16px}</style>
<script language="JScript">
function runCommand(cmd){
 var shell=new ActiveXObject("WScript.Shell"), fso=new ActiveXObject("Scripting.FileSystemObject");
 var here=unescape(document.location.pathname).replace(/^\//,"").replace(/\//g,"\");
 var root=fso.GetParentFolderName(fso.GetParentFolderName(fso.GetParentFolderName(here)));
 var engine=root+"\platform\recon-sync\recon-sync-engine.ps1";
 var command='powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "'+engine+'" -Command '+cmd+' -RepoRoot "'+root+'" -Json';
 document.getElementById("result").innerText="Running "+cmd+"...";
 var proc=shell.Exec(command), out=proc.StdOut.ReadAll(), err=proc.StdErr.ReadAll();
 document.getElementById("result").innerText=out+(err?"\nSTDERR:\n"+err:"")+"\nExit code: "+proc.ExitCode;
}
</script></head><body><h1>Research OS — Recon-Sync</h1>
<p>Status and audit can run without a canonical remote. Sync refuses dirty worktrees. Recover currently verifies evidence only and does not restore files.</p>
<button onclick="runCommand('status')">Status</button><button onclick="runCommand('audit')">Audit</button><button onclick="runCommand('evidence')">Generate evidence</button><button onclick="runCommand('verify')">Verify canonical</button><button onclick="runCommand('sync')">Sync worktree</button><button onclick="runCommand('recover')">Verify recovery evidence</button>
<div id="result">Ready.</div></body></html>
